Backport of upstream wine commit 1897b27f25 (wine-11.18, "winex11.drv:
Use memmove in strip_driver_extra."): the modes are compacted in place,
so source and destination overlap once more than one mode is listed.
OpenBSD libc aborts on overlapping memcpy ("backwards memcpy" in syslog);
under Xvfb this killed explorer.exe and a DXVK D3D11 test while the
display devices were being enumerated.

Index: dlls/winex11.drv/display.c
--- dlls/winex11.drv/display.c.orig
+++ dlls/winex11.drv/display.c
@@ -162,7 +162,7 @@ static void strip_driver_extra( DEVMODEW
     {
         next = NEXT_DEVMODEW(mode);
         mode->dmDriverExtra = 0;
-        memcpy( modes + i, mode, sizeof(*mode) );
+        memmove( modes + i, mode, sizeof(*mode) );
     }
 }
 
